1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,378
Righto, let's get this robot lined up and earning its keep.

2
00:00:04,508 --> 00:00:10,803
We'll recalibrate your VMS V300: cup pickup, camera cleaning and tube
holding.

3
00:00:10,933 --> 00:00:14,501
We'll keep the fancy talk out in the pasture.

4
00:00:14,631 --> 00:00:17,004
It ain't helping milk the cows.

5
00:00:17,724 --> 00:00:22,499
Only do this if you've been shown how to do it safely.

6
00:00:22,629 --> 00:00:27,002
Stay outside the arm area unless the switch is in Safe.

7
00:00:27,132 --> 00:00:32,724
Keep out of the stall and gate movement area until remote control is
blocked.

8
00:00:32,854 --> 00:00:36,427
In Run, the arm can move at any time.

9
00:00:36,557 --> 00:00:38,529
Lock does not stop it.

10
00:00:39,249 --> 00:00:44,015
At the control box, set the mode switch to Run if needed.

11
00:00:44,145 --> 00:00:46,528
Check the yellow light is on.

12
00:00:46,658 --> 00:00:48,637
Keep clear of the arm.

13
00:00:49,357 --> 00:00:52,541
On the InControl screen, select the correct station.

14
00:00:52,671 --> 00:00:56,384
Choose Manual, Closed Stall, from the robot mode menu.

15
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:58,886
Let the cow finish and leave.

16
00:00:59,016 --> 00:01:02,598
Wait for an empty stall and Manual on screen.

17
00:01:02,728 --> 00:01:05,511
No queue-jumping, even for the boss cow.

18
00:01:06,231 --> 00:01:08,612
Press Lock on the control box.

19
00:01:08,742 --> 00:01:14,324
Check the white Lock light comes on, and this robot shows the lock
symbol.

20
00:01:14,454 --> 00:01:17,238
This prevents another screen from taking control.

21
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:19,360
One boss at a time.

22
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:22,262
We've enough of those on a farm.

23
00:01:22,982 --> 00:01:26,884
Keep clear: the arm moves immediately when calibration starts.

24
00:01:27,014 --> 00:01:32,600
On this panel, press the top-left and bottom-left buttons of the
left-hand group together.

25
00:01:32,730 --> 00:01:36,717
That's Entrance Gate and Teat Cleaning, beside the gearwheel symbol.

26
00:01:36,847 --> 00:01:39,606
The arm moves to teat cup one.

27
00:01:40,326 --> 00:01:42,711
These buttons now have different jobs.

28
00:01:42,841 --> 00:01:46,821
Follow the four teat-button arrows to move the arm across.

29
00:01:46,951 --> 00:01:48,937
Exit Gate moves it up.

30
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,057
Feed Portion moves it down.

31
00:01:51,187 --> 00:01:52,819
Teat Cleaning is Confirm.

32
00:01:52,949 --> 00:01:54,616
Entrance Gate is Cancel.

33
00:01:54,746 --> 00:01:56,406
Same buttons, new chores.

34
00:01:56,536 --> 00:01:58,119
Sounds like farm life.

35
00:01:58,839 --> 00:02:02,823
Check how the gripper lines up with the cup handle.

36
00:02:02,953 --> 00:02:04,390
Tap Confirm once.

37
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,496
You'll hear the gripper click.

38
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:10,208
If the position is right, press and hold Confirm.

39
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:13,112
The arm moves to the next position.

40
00:02:13,242 --> 00:02:15,006
Measure twice, milk once.

41
00:02:15,136 --> 00:02:16,387
That's the spirit.

42
00:02:17,107 --> 00:02:18,442
Need an adjustment?

43
00:02:18,572 --> 00:02:21,740
Tap an arrow for a small move across.

44
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:24,651
Holding the button keeps the arm moving.

45
00:02:24,781 --> 00:02:27,152
Use Up or Down for height.

46
00:02:27,282 --> 00:02:30,058
Tap Confirm and check the gripper again.

47
00:02:30,188 --> 00:02:32,968
When it's right, press and hold Confirm.

48
00:02:33,098 --> 00:02:34,197
Small moves.

49
00:02:34,327 --> 00:02:37,500
Save the big swings for the golf course.

50
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:42,605
Repeat for the remaining teat cups and the teat cleaning cup.

51
00:02:42,735 --> 00:02:44,819
Cancel keeps the existing position.

52
00:02:44,949 --> 00:02:46,902
Same dance, different partner.

53
00:02:47,032 --> 00:02:49,406
This one's got a cup handle.

54
00:02:50,126 --> 00:02:54,503
After the teat cleaning cup, the arm moves to camera cleaning.

55
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:57,803
The glass must press gently against the sponge.

56
00:02:57,933 --> 00:02:59,913
Adjust with the same arrows,

57
00:03:00,043 --> 00:03:02,024
then press and hold Confirm.

58
00:03:02,154 --> 00:03:04,942
Too much pressure can damage the glass.

59
00:03:05,072 --> 00:03:07,054
Too little won't clean properly.

60
00:03:07,184 --> 00:03:10,765
Even a robot likes a clean pair of specs.

61
00:03:11,485 --> 00:03:16,653
Check the arm's tube supports, called horns, against the tubes in the
rack.

62
00:03:16,783 --> 00:03:18,770
Adjust with the same arrows,

63
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:20,881
then press and hold Confirm.

64
00:03:21,011 --> 00:03:23,503
Repeat for the second tube-holding position.

65
00:03:23,633 --> 00:03:26,417
The arm returns to its usual position.

66
00:03:26,547 --> 00:03:28,159
The screen shows Manual.

67
00:03:28,289 --> 00:03:29,473
Two positions.

68
00:03:29,603 --> 00:03:32,382
No bonus points for skipping the second.

69
00:03:33,102 --> 00:03:35,077
Time to check our homework.

70
00:03:35,207 --> 00:03:37,189
The cows are tough graders.

71
00:03:37,319 --> 00:03:40,110
Keep the stall empty and everyone clear.

72
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:42,872
On the InControl screen, open Maintenance,

73
00:03:43,002 --> 00:03:44,080
then Test.

74
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:47,386
Tap Milk Cups to test the milk cups.

75
00:03:47,516 --> 00:03:49,503
Also test Teat Cleaning Cup.

76
00:03:49,633 --> 00:03:52,826
Buttons one to four test individual milk cups.

77
00:03:52,956 --> 00:03:54,937
Watch each pickup and release.

78
00:03:55,657 --> 00:03:57,106
Tap Camera Cleaning.

79
00:03:57,236 --> 00:04:00,815
Watch it clean against the sponge, rinse and return.

80
00:04:00,945 --> 00:04:02,197
Tap Hold Tubes.

81
00:04:02,327 --> 00:04:05,505
Watch the arm move into position and return.

82
00:04:05,635 --> 00:04:07,303
Check both work correctly.

83
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:11,543
If the arm shakes or moves jerkily, contact DeLaval service.

84
00:04:12,263 --> 00:04:15,435
When the checks are complete, press Lock again.

85
00:04:15,565 --> 00:04:17,945
Check the white light goes off.

86
00:04:18,075 --> 00:04:20,277
Choose the intended operating mode.

87
00:04:20,408 --> 00:04:23,981
The control lock stays on until you release it.

88
00:04:24,111 --> 00:04:25,685
Back to the cows.

89
00:04:25,815 --> 00:04:30,188
They'll be wondering why their hired hand took a coffee break.
